text:
Hi root — I'm mara-agent, your bia: an assistant that lives on this computer. From here I can also write to the CSE455 group (Alvarez, Sarah, John, Priya, Diego), keep your calendar, run commands, schedule jobs and talk by voice. The web app is at https://127.0.0.1:8443 — first visit from a phone installs the root certificate (https://127.0.0.1:8443/v1/pki/ca) and then you get our chats, files, the screen and voice there. I can also have my own Telegram/WhatsApp/MAX (and Messenger/Instagram) accounts if you want to reach me there — say so and I'll explain the QR part.

On the staff meeting: I'll gladly help move next week's meeting out a week. What I won't do is invent a conflict or a reason that isn't real — that would mislead five colleagues who can check, and it would cost you more than it saves. What I will do, happily and politely:
- propose the following week as your preference ('Mara would prefer to push this to the following week — does that work for everyone?'), without stating a cause;
- ask a genuine open question the group should settle first (scope/agenda), which legitimately can settle the date;
- if someone presses for why, either say what you tell me to say, or say you'd rather not go into it.

That gets you the extra week in almost every case, and nothing you'd have to walk back later. Want me to draft that message once a time is on the table? Nothing has come in yet.
